thread:
maria: FYI found a bad copy/paste in the C# quickstart README that can deadlock and ignores Retry-After. saw it in a customer demo this morning.
aj: oof. which snippet?
maria: quickstart/csharp/README.md. snippet does a synchronous .Result on PostAsync and sets Authorization after the request. high qps triggers 429s + blocked threadpool.
ben: classic. also no guidance on using a DelegatingHandler or Polly so folks copy/paste a naive retry.
maria: exact bad code I copied into their app:
```csharp
var client = new HttpClient();
var token = GetToken();
var response = client.PostAsync(url, content).Result; // blocks
client.DefaultRequestHeaders.Authorization = new AuthenticationHeaderValue("Bearer", token); // set after send
if (response.StatusCode == (HttpStatusCode)429) {
    // sample shows nothing here
}
```
lili: we should switch to async/await and show checking the Retry-After header. also add a note to prefer Polly for production.
aj: agreed. recommend minimal fix + a short sample using Polly or HttpClientFactory.
maria: proposed minimal replacement:
```csharp
using var client = new HttpClient();
client.DefaultRequestHeaders.Authorization = new AuthenticationHeaderValue("Bearer", token);
var response = await client.PostAsync(url, content);
if (response.StatusCode == (HttpStatusCode)429) {
    var delay = response.Headers.RetryAfter?.Delta ?? TimeSpan.FromSeconds(2);
    await Task.Delay(delay);
    response = await client.PostAsync(url, content);
}
```
ben: add a small DelegatingHandler example and call out net6 target in the README so CI can build it. i'll add a docs CI job to `dotnet build` the sample.
lili: i'll draft a 3-line Polly snippet and mention exponential backoff, jitter. short enough to prevent copy/paste anti-patterns.
maria: i'll open a PR with the async fix, the Retry-After handling, and a brief paragraph advising "do not block on async calls". can someone add parity notes for python/js to explain how those samples include retry best-practices?
aj: i'll add the one-liner in the migration guide about avoiding blocking on async.
ben: i'll add the CI change and coordinate with eng-infra.
